 R←Test_UC_027(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;target;rc;msg;result;stop
⍝ Runs ]CloneRepo with -dry and a two-digit -depth=. Three defects met in this one call:
⍝ * -depth= had no numeric default, so "10" arrived as text and <CloneRepo>'s `0≠depth` was a
⍝   LENGTH ERROR (with -depth=5 it worked by luck)
⍝ * -dry created the target folder before establishing that it had nothing to do
⍝ * the command was sent through project establishment it does not need, so without an open
⍝   project the user was asked whether to act on the current directory
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 stop←0

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 target←tempDir,'/target'

 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'CloneRepo aplteam/APLGit2 "',target,'" -dry -depth=10'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'--depth 10'⍷∊result
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'clone'⍷∊result
 →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕NEXISTS target          ⍝ A dry run must not create anything

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
